+### Navbar classes
+
+The navbar key ships in its own partial in the components layer: the bar, the brand, the list and
+its current and open links, the menu it holds, the text, the collapsible content, the toggler and
+its icon, the scrolling list, the expand ramp with the expanded offcanvas panel, and the dark
+retunes. The partial loads between the nav partial and the card partial, at the barrel's Bootstrap
+order. The container combinators the key records ship from the container partial, whose own key
+records them too, so the navbar partial writes none of them. The `.navbar-light` class is the
+release's deprecated light form and emits no rule there, so it has none here.
+
+Every value the partial paints is Bootstrap 5.3.8's own, apart from the forced-colors focus outline
+§ Additions records. A length reads the Veneer scale token that already resolves to it, so the bar's
+block inset, the brand's end margin, the list's block inset, the expanded link inset, the text's
+block inset, and the toggler's insets answer to the `--vn-factor-density` factor, and the brand and
+toggler type read the `--vn-size-5` token. The brand's `0.3125rem` block inset keeps the release's
+literal, because no scale token resolves to it. The toggler's `0.25rem` focus width keeps the
+release's literal too, because the published focus width is a narrower ring. A light color is the
+release's own expression over the `--bs-emphasis-color-rgb` channels, so a plain bar's text follows the mode it sits in. The toggler
+icon is the release's data URI in each mode, read from the Sass glyph maps the `_tokens.scss`
+partial declares, because a data URI cannot read a custom property.
+
+Each `--bs-navbar-*` property is declared on the `.navbar` class, so the bar itself is where a
+consumer retunes one, and the same override on an ancestor is shadowed. The `.navbar-nav` class
+retunes the nav link slots to the bar's colors, so a link inside the list paints from the navbar
+variables through the nav partial's own rules, the current link and a toggle carrying the `show`
+class take the active color, and the list sits flush with the bar's edge. The `.navbar-text` class
+takes the list's block inset and the bar's text color, and a link inside it takes the active color.
+
+A bar without an expand class is collapsed at every width. Its collapsible content hides while it
+carries the `collapse` class without the `show` class, and adding the `show` class opens it on a row
+of its own under the brand and the toggler, where a menu in the list opens in the column's flow and
+pushes the links after it down. Each `.navbar-expand-sm`, `.navbar-expand-md`, `.navbar-expand-lg`,
+`.navbar-expand-xl`, and `.navbar-expand-xxl` class expands the bar from its boundary up, and the
+`.navbar-expand` class expands it at every width. An expanded bar lays its content out in one row,
+runs the list in a row with the `--bs-navbar-nav-link-padding-x` inset on each link, hangs a menu
+over the content again, lets the scrolling list overflow, hides the toggler, and shows the
+collapsible content while its collapse class would hide it, because that rule carries the
+release's `!important` flag.
+
+The expanded bar also turns an offcanvas panel into part of its row: the panel stops being
+positioned, grows into the row, and drops its header, and the release's `!important` flags on its
+size, visibility, fill, border, and transform win over the hidden state the panel's own classes
+write. Those rules ship ahead of the panel's own partial. The Navbar region renders no offcanvas
+panel until the Offcanvas unit of B-MODAL … B-CAROUSEL ships that partial, and the proof reads the
+rules on elements of its own.
+
+The `.navbar-nav-scroll` class clamps the list to the height the `--bs-scroll-height` property
+names, and to three quarters of the viewport while no scope sets that property; the list scrolls
+inside that height.
+
+The `.navbar-dark` class and the `data-bs-theme="dark"` attribute on the bar itself each retune the
+bar's colors and its toggler to the release's white literals, written as mixes over the
